\begin_layout Standard
All files come in triplets for each observer:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Alice,
 blue,
 west end of Innsbruck campus; 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bob,
 red,
 east end of campus.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Dasta files for each observer (alice.zip,
 bob.zip).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
*_V.dat
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
A list of photon arrival times where the arm time has been subtracted.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
IEEE-8bit double precision numbers in Big Endian form naturally sorted ascendingly.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Actual time resolution is 10-10seconds,
 but accuracy is only 0.5 ns.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
*_C.dat
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The apparatus setting and outcome for each photon detection is encoded as 16-bit integers in Big Endian form,
 each 16-bit number showing:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
the detector (0=vertical,
 1=horizontal with respect to the polarizer) that fired in its LSB and
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
the position of the switch (0=no rotation,
 1=45° rotation) in the next to LSB.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Inspection of data indicates that the setting codes are in bit 15 and 16 of the number:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bit 16:
 detector that fired,
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bit 15:
 switch position.
\end_layout

